# rects sit far apart along x.
#
# A `TRUNK_*+MST` hybrid COPIES its seed trunk and then replaces some branch
# stubs with inter-block MST edges.  Since the copy carries the seed's OVER
# connection metal, CLAUDE.md claimed the hybrids "inherit the seed trunk's
# per-rect metal".  They did not — three passes the hybrid path runs and
# `add_trunk` does not were quietly taking it back out, each of them on the same
# false premise that a block's rects are interchangeable covers:
